{
  "fixture_id": "x-11-source-extra-merge",
  "fixture_kind": "record",
  "case": "Two systems describe one identity and each fills `source.extra` with its own keys — the bag merges key by key, so Zenodo's resource subtype survives DataCite's higher precedence",
  "note": "The bug this fixture exists to stop coming back. `extra` is a BAG of fields, and each source fills it with keys only that source has. Composing several systems by wholesale replacement meant the highest-precedence system's bag deleted every other system's — so a record scraped by both DataCite (precedence 10) and Zenodo (30) kept `datacite_types` and silently lost `zenodo_resource_type`, which is the most specific classification signal the catalogue has: Zenodo states a type AND a subtype where DataCite's copy of the very same record flattens both to \"Text\". The consequence was visible on the site: a project deliverable filed as a bare \"Publication\", and 54 records in \"Other > Other\" that were really presentations, posters and meeting minutes. Order is deliberate — Zenodo first, DataCite second — because the dangerous direction is the higher-precedence source arriving last. Note what precedence still decides: `title` is DataCite's, because DataCite outranks Zenodo on scalars. Only the bag merges.",
  "raw": "raw/x-11-source-extra-merge.json",
